# What's New in AG Grid 33.2

*Author: Kiril Matev*  
*Date: 24 March 2025*

AG Grid Enterprise 33.2 is a minor release that introduces several new features and enhancements, improving performance and accessibility.

Key additions in this release:

1. Find
2. Tree Data Self-Referencing Records
3. Status Bar Value Formatting
4. Row Spanning Pagination Support
5. Accessibility Improvements

Please note that AG Grid 33.2 has no breaking changes from AG Grid 33.x. If you're already using AG Grid 33.x, this upgrade doesn't require any changes to your codebase.

We recommend reviewing the release notes when planning to update to this version.

## Find

AG Grid 33.2 introduces a new "Find" feature, allowing users to search for content within grid cells. This enables users to quickly locate all occurrences of a string across all grid cells and rows without filtering out rows that don't contain the searched content. The matching text in grid cells is styled similarly to the way browsers highlight search matches, making this feature intuitive for end-users.

## Tree Data Self-Referencing Records

This release enables tree data to display hierarchical self-referencing data where each row provides a reference to its parent. This new feature eliminates the need to transform the data before providing it to the grid, allowing users to interact directly with hierarchical data using AG Grid's standard feature set.

## Status Bar Value Formatting

AG Grid 33.2 adds the ability to format values shown in the status bar panels. This enhancement allows for better presentation of status bar values, ensuring correct decimal fraction number formatting and enabling customization of large number displays to make them more concise and meaningful to users.

## Row Spanning Pagination Support

The row spanning feature has been improved to add full support for row pagination. This enhancement enables the grid to display a more sparse view of the data, allowing users to more easily identify rows with identical cell values in a column, even when using row pagination.

## Accessibility Improvements

AG Grid 33.2 enhances accessibility support in the columns tool panel, allowing users to reorder columns in the columns list, as well as in the row groups, pivot, and values panels using the keyboard. This improvement is part of our ongoing efforts to enhance accessibility support, enabling the grid to generate appropriate announcements for screen readers and provide more intuitive and comprehensive keyboard navigation.

## Summary

AG Grid 33.2 is a significant minor version that adds important end-user features and improvements in performance, accessibility, and quality. We highly recommend upgrading to this new version to benefit from these enhancements.

We suggest reviewing the release notes when planning to upgrade and seeing the full list of changes in our changelog.

As always, we’re keen to help you upgrade and to hear your feedback.

Happy coding!